                  <provenance type="#e" source="320"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_29">Bardney, Lincolnshire.
                        Benedictine abbey of St Peter, St Paul, and St Oswald</orgName><p>Given by
                        Roger de Fuldon, archdeacon of Lincoln (1255/6–77), 'deo et S. Oswaldo et
                        abbati \Petro de Bartona/ et conuentui de Bardoneia' (fol. i verso). Later
                        belonged to Tattershall (q.v.) but was seen by Leland at Bardney. 14th-cent.
                        Bardney cauciones, one 'ciste S. Iohannis', 1 Feb. 1389 (fol.
                     182v).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Tattershall College</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Bought by Roger from Galfridus capellanus,
                     brother of Henry, vicar of N. Elkington (Lincs).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">King Henry VIII (Westminster inventory of
                     1542, H2.784)</provenance>
               <provenance type="#e" source="5442"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_539">Tattershall,
                        Lincolnshire. Collegiate church of the Holy Trinity and St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>'Collegium de Tatteshall' (fol. 4r)</p><p>'Hunc librum emit
                        Gigur de executoribus magistri More [!]' (fol. 1v, s. xv
                        in.).</p><p>Formerly belonged to Bardney (q. v.) and perhas recovered later
                        by that house.</p></provenance>
